.TH CLIPHIST 1 "2026-10-07" "cliphist 0.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cliphist \- clipboard history manager for Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cliphist
[\fIoptions\fR]
.I command
[\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cliphist
records clipboard changes to a persistent database and allows recalling
them later.
Both text and binary data (including images) are supported.
Clipboard entries are preserved byte-for-byte, including leading and
trailing whitespace.
.PP
.B cliphist
has no built-in picker UI.
Instead it emits tab-separated output intended to be piped through an
external menu program such as
.BR dmenu (1),
.BR rofi (1),
.BR fzf (1),
or
.BR fuzzel (1).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B store
Read stdin and append it to the history database.
Intended to be driven by
.BR wl-paste (1)
in watch mode.
If the environment variable
.B CLIPBOARD_STATE
is set to
.I sensitive
the entry is silently dropped; if set to
.I clear
the most recently stored entry is removed.
.TP
.BI "list " "[\-fields \fIfields\fR] [\fIid\fR]"
Print clipboard history to stdout as TSV, newest first.
Each line contains the columns requested by
.BR \-fields .
The default output is
.IR id \t preview .
If a numeric
.I id
is supplied, only that entry is printed.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-fields " fields"
Comma-separated list of columns to include.
Valid column names are
.BR id ,
.BR preview ,
.BR timestamp ,
.BR mime ,
and
.BR format .
Keep
.B id
first if the output will be piped into
.B decode
or
.BR delete .
Default:
.IR id,preview .
.RE
.TP
.BI "decode " "[id]"
Write the raw bytes of a clipboard entry to stdout.
Reads a
.BI id \t...
line from stdin unless a numeric
.I id
is provided directly.
Use this to restore an entry to the clipboard via
.BR wl-copy (1).
.TP
.B delete
Delete one or more entries.
Reads
.BI id \t...
lines from stdin (as produced by
.BR list ).
.TP
.BI "delete\-query " query
Delete all entries whose raw content contains
.IR query .
.TP
.BI "wipe " "[\-older\-than \fIduration\fR]"
Delete all entries (and compact the database afterwards).
.RS
.TP
.BI \-older\-than " duration"
Only delete entries older than
.IR duration .
The value is a Go duration string; because Go does not define a day unit,
days must be expressed in hours (e.g.\&
.I 720h
for 30 days).
Entries that predate timestamp tracking are treated as infinitely old and
are always removed when this flag is used.
.RE
.TP
.B compact
Compact the database file in place, reclaiming space freed by deletions.
.TP
.B version
Print the cliphist version and current option values, then exit.
.SH OPTIONS
Global options may be placed before the command name.
Each option may also be set via an environment variable or a line in the
config file (see
.B CONFIGURATION
below).
.TP
.BI \-db\-path " path"
Path to the database file.
Default:
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/cliphist/db .
.TP
.BI \-config\-path " path"
Path to the configuration file.
Default:
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cliphist/config .
This option cannot be set via the config file itself.
.TP
.BI \-max\-items " n"
Maximum number of entries to retain.
Oldest entries are removed when the limit is exceeded.
Default:
.IR 750 .
.TP
.BI \-max\-dedupe\-search " n"
Number of recent entries to scan when checking for duplicates before
storing a new entry.
Default:
.IR 100 .
.TP
.BI \-max\-store\-size " size"
Maximum size of a clipboard item to store.
Accepts a number of bytes or a suffixed value such as
.IR 5MB ,
.IR 10MiB ,
or
.IR 1GB .
Default:
.IR 5MB .
.TP
.BI \-min\-store\-length " n"
Minimum number of grapheme clusters a text entry must contain to be stored.
Default:
.I 0
(no minimum).
.TP
.BI \-preview\-width " n"
Maximum number of characters shown in the
.I preview
field of
.BR list .
Default:
.IR 100 .
.SH CONFIGURATION
Options can be read from a plain-text config file.
The default location is
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cliphist/config ;
override with
.B \-config\-path
or
.BR CLIPHIST_CONFIG_PATH .
.PP
Each non-empty, non-comment line has the form:
.PP
.RS
.I key value
.RE
.PP
Lines beginning with
.B #
are comments.
Example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
# keep two years of history
max\-items 1000
max\-dedupe\-search 200
.fi
.RE
.PP
CLI flags take precedence over environment variables, which take precedence
over config file values.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLIPHIST_DB_PATH
Equivalent to
.BR \-db\-path .
.TP
.B CLIPHIST_CONFIG_PATH
Equivalent to
.BR \-config\-path .
.TP
.B CLIPHIST_MAX_ITEMS
Equivalent to
.BR \-max\-items .
.TP
.B CLIPHIST_MAX_DEDEUPE_SEARCH
Equivalent to
.BR \-max\-dedupe\-search .
.TP
.B CLIPHIST_MAX_STORE_SIZE
Equivalent to
.BR \-max\-store\-size .
.TP
.B CLIPHIST_MIN_STORE_LENGTH
Equivalent to
.BR \-min\-store\-length .
.TP
.B CLIPHIST_PREVIEW_WIDTH
Equivalent to
.BR \-preview\-width .
.TP
.B CLIPBOARD_STATE
Set by
.BR wl-paste (1)
in watch mode.
When set to
.I sensitive
the incoming clipboard data is discarded without storing.
When set to
.I clear
the most recently stored entry is deleted.
.TP
.B CLIPBOARD_TYPE
Set by
.BR wl-paste (1)
in watch mode (requires wl-clipboard > 2.3.0).
Used to record the MIME type of a stored entry.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/cliphist/db
Default database location (bbolt key-value store).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cliphist/config
Default configuration file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Listen for clipboard changes
Start once per session (e.g. from your compositor config):
.PP
.RS
.nf
wl\-paste \-\-watch cliphist store
.fi
.RE
.PP
To capture both text and images explicitly:
.PP
.RS
.nf
wl\-paste \-\-type text  \-\-watch cliphist store
wl\-paste \-\-type image \-\-watch cliphist store
.fi
.RE
.SS Restore an entry to the clipboard
.RS
.nf
cliphist list | dmenu | cliphist decode | wl\-copy
cliphist list | fzf \-\-no\-sort | cliphist decode | wl\-copy
cliphist list | rofi \-dmenu | cliphist decode | wl\-copy
cliphist list | fuzzel \-\-dmenu | cliphist decode | wl\-copy
cliphist list | wofi \-S dmenu | cliphist decode | wl\-copy
.fi
.RE
.SS Hide the ID column from the picker
.RS
.nf
# fzf
cliphist list | fzf \-d $'\\t' \-\-with\-nth 2 | cliphist decode | wl\-copy
# rofi
cliphist list | rofi \-dmenu \-display\-columns 2 | cliphist decode | wl\-copy
# fuzzel
cliphist list | fuzzel \-\-dmenu \-\-with\-nth 2 | cliphist decode | wl\-copy
.fi
.RE
.SS Delete an entry
.RS
.nf
cliphist list | dmenu | cliphist delete
cliphist delete\-query "secret text"
.fi
.RE
.SS Inspect entry metadata
.RS
.nf
cliphist list \-fields id,mime,preview
cliphist list \-fields id,timestamp
cliphist list \-fields mime,format 123
.fi
.RE
.SS Expire old entries (run from a timer)
.RS
.nf
cliphist wipe \-older\-than 720h
.fi
.RE
.SS Use a non-default database path
.RS
.nf
cliphist \-db\-path /tmp/clipboard.db list
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wl\-paste (1),
.BR wl\-copy (1),
.BR dmenu (1),
.BR rofi (1),
.BR fzf (1),
.BR fuzzel (1),
.BR wofi (1)
